# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## Project Overview

**Shopping AI** — A FastAPI-based REST API that provides AI-powered product search using a keyword/brand/model scoring algorithm.

## Running the Server

```bash
source venv/bin/activate
uvicorn backend.app.main:app --reload
```

The API runs on `http://localhost:8000` by default. FastAPI auto-generates interactive docs at `/docs`.

## Testing the API

```bash
curl http://localhost:8000/
curl "http://localhost:8000/search?q=sony+headphones"
```

## Architecture

Three core modules:

- **`backend/app/main.py`** — FastAPI app with two endpoints: `GET /` (health check) and `GET /search?q=` (product search). The search endpoint scores all products, filters at score ≥ 20, and returns sorted results.
- **`backend/app/products.py`** — In-memory product database (hardcoded list of dicts with id, brand, model, name, category, price, store fields).
- **`backend/app/product_matching.py`** — Scoring engine: `normalize(text)` strips non-alphanumeric chars; `calculate_match_score(query, product)` returns 0–100 using weighted rules: brand match (+30), full model match (+70), model fragment ≥3 chars (+50), query words in name (+5 each), brand+model fragment combo (+20).

There is no database, no authentication, and no frontend — this is a minimal proof-of-concept.

## Dependencies

Dependencies are managed via the `venv/` virtual environment at the project root. There is no `requirements.txt`; if adding packages, pin them and create one.

Key packages: `fastapi`, `uvicorn`, `pydantic`.
